          "type": "turn",
          "question": "From what age does guidance describe screening for type 2 diabetes?",
          "answer": "The guidelines recommend screening for type 2 diabetes in all adults starting from age 35. Additionally, younger adults who are overweight or obese and have at least one other risk factor should be screened. This risk factor could include having a first-degree relative with diabetes, being part of a high-risk racial or ethnic group, having established cardiovascular disease, high blood pressure, certain lipid levels, polycystic ovary syndrome, physical inactivity, or a history of gestational diabetes. \n\nThis information is drawn from the \"National diabetes association standards of care and preventive services guidance (educational summary)\" on type 2 diabetes screening.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
